[{:db/id 17592186092185 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e321af2f-d67a-5dc4-a077-c6060845ea99"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092025 :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y-2z=-2 \\\\ -3y+z=-2 \\\\ 3x-7y+3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $A \\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Given that $\\mathbf x = \\langle x,y,z\\rangle$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n![](images/22/220e8838850356768215ed74aefc469edbdc99aa50b9116729329f0e818d6978.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092186 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0807a9e2-ba3b-5d6e-8562-a580bc61f62a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092026 :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}3y+x+z=0 \\\\ z+4y-5=2 \\\\ 1+2x-y=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are in the correct order and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y+z=0 \\\\ 0x+4y+z=7 \\\\ 2x-y+0z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n![](images/e8/e816a0fcde823bc6f6e88dff0a02c1877275cbed75757c1eb366fb224629127e.svg)\n\nNow, the solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is given by $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$ So, we compute $A^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1*: Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1)-3(-2)+(-8) \\\\  & =1+6-8 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2*: Compute the matrix of minors.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3*:  Find the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](images/be/beb80ea3185fc723c294313b63274554ec8af3531ed5643173a6127c59a21bb3.svg)\n\n*Step 4*: Transpose the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](images/e6/e6fac5dd0a9918a03ce7c14e9cd05a06c6d11e95346f261ec75d6ebea09de1d6.svg)\n\n*Step 5*: Apply the inverse matrix formula.\n\n![](images/72/72b9d627d372d7a64a271b555b0d4cbb89b2bf9d602cdec64b1d8987a5e21521.svg)\n\nFinally, we can calculate the solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -33\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3,$ $y=10,$ $z=-33.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092187 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0c58ffa5-e4d4-5bf5-8b35-8a71f48534ba"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e321af2f-d67a-5dc4-a077-c6060845ea99" :question/id #uuid "e321af2f-d67a-5dc4-a077-c6060845ea99" :question/math-academy-id "q-78553" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+z=3 \\\\ x-2y+z=1 \\\\ 2x-y+2z=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=-1,y=1,z=4.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=-1+1+4=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c0e50419-c826-5a89-9337-910bb9a469c2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c0e50419-c826-5a89-9337-910bb9a469c2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0e50419-c826-5a89-9337-910bb9a469c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ed96fe73-34bc-5554-8fe0-b110d7f3f6b3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b90c4ae0-c1ef-52b6-b3de-1cbcb9e94c5e" "answer-f3dc6b18-74c4-595b-92c7-e48fa955a38e" "answer-d60be700-46fb-5903-a3f8-cfb1794eaf06" "answer-ed96fe73-34bc-5554-8fe0-b110d7f3f6b3" "answer-4fc306a8-65be-5769-9f23-972df29a47cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b90c4ae0-c1ef-52b6-b3de-1cbcb9e94c5e" :answer/id #uuid "b90c4ae0-c1ef-52b6-b3de-1cbcb9e94c5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3dc6b18-74c4-595b-92c7-e48fa955a38e" :answer/id #uuid "f3dc6b18-74c4-595b-92c7-e48fa955a38e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d60be700-46fb-5903-a3f8-cfb1794eaf06" :answer/id #uuid "d60be700-46fb-5903-a3f8-cfb1794eaf06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed96fe73-34bc-5554-8fe0-b110d7f3f6b3" :answer/id #uuid "ed96fe73-34bc-5554-8fe0-b110d7f3f6b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fc306a8-65be-5769-9f23-972df29a47cd" :answer/id #uuid "4fc306a8-65be-5769-9f23-972df29a47cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0807a9e2-ba3b-5d6e-8562-a580bc61f62a" :question/id #uuid "0807a9e2-ba3b-5d6e-8562-a580bc61f62a" :question/math-academy-id "q-104515" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z=-1 \\\\ 3x-z=5+3y \\\\ 3z-2y=6-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind  $x+y+z.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z=-1 \\\\ 3x-3y-z=5 \\\\ x-2y+3z=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+(-2)|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(-9-2)-(9+1)-2(-6+3) \\\\  & =-22-10+6 \\\\  & =-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 10 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-11 & -10 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 5 \\\\ -7 & -4 & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -10 & 8 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -10 & 8 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -10 & 8 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}-26 \\\\ 26 \\\\ -26\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x+y+z=1-1+1=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d554649a-905d-57c6-af27-cc40c4c45a3a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d554649a-905d-57c6-af27-cc40c4c45a3a" :answer-field/id #uuid "d554649a-905d-57c6-af27-cc40c4c45a3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-28126022-8f20-5f62-8417-0685db76f23b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3b9511ec-b4f9-5c7b-b596-beebd0bcb054" "answer-274c794a-3cbb-5dc2-bbb2-1f1131f70f1e" "answer-28126022-8f20-5f62-8417-0685db76f23b" "answer-0597b830-4974-5289-8d3c-e5ddb2d894f7" "answer-039d5f33-dfa0-51c2-93be-2b7000137d8a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b9511ec-b4f9-5c7b-b596-beebd0bcb054" :answer/id #uuid "3b9511ec-b4f9-5c7b-b596-beebd0bcb054" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-274c794a-3cbb-5dc2-bbb2-1f1131f70f1e" :answer/id #uuid "274c794a-3cbb-5dc2-bbb2-1f1131f70f1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28126022-8f20-5f62-8417-0685db76f23b" :answer/id #uuid "28126022-8f20-5f62-8417-0685db76f23b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0597b830-4974-5289-8d3c-e5ddb2d894f7" :answer/id #uuid "0597b830-4974-5289-8d3c-e5ddb2d894f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-039d5f33-dfa0-51c2-93be-2b7000137d8a" :answer/id #uuid "039d5f33-dfa0-51c2-93be-2b7000137d8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186237810 :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y+z=6 \\\\ 4x+7y+2z=0 \\\\ 3x+y+z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-0c58ffa5-e4d4-5bf5-8b35-8a71f48534ba" :question/id #uuid "0c58ffa5-e4d4-5bf5-8b35-8a71f48534ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-78565" :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation $B\\,x=A\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $2\\times 2$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $2\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${B}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $B\\,x=A\\,d$ by ${B}^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}B\\,x & ={B}^{-1}A\\,d \\\\ {I}_{2}\\,x & ={B}^{-1}A\\,d \\\\ x & ={B}^{-1}A\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3722cf83-66cd-54b2-a5b1-3a7fa87b1c56"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3722cf83-66cd-54b2-a5b1-3a7fa87b1c56" :answer-field/id #uuid "3722cf83-66cd-54b2-a5b1-3a7fa87b1c56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8afcf5b9-6023-5abe-9e32-15e5a0353825" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7539810a-78b4-56d6-8b1e-ddb5c34343c1" "answer-e12ef937-d966-5968-a2bc-5cb307c85739" "answer-3a64a01b-e02d-535d-a027-6746b0121352" "answer-b14cf1e4-785f-5b17-867e-45e5d7cc5a9f" "answer-8afcf5b9-6023-5abe-9e32-15e5a0353825"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7539810a-78b4-56d6-8b1e-ddb5c34343c1" :answer/id #uuid "7539810a-78b4-56d6-8b1e-ddb5c34343c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=A\\,d\\,B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e12ef937-d966-5968-a2bc-5cb307c85739" :answer/id #uuid "e12ef937-d966-5968-a2bc-5cb307c85739" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=A\\,d\\,{B}^{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a64a01b-e02d-535d-a027-6746b0121352" :answer/id #uuid "3a64a01b-e02d-535d-a027-6746b0121352" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=A{B}^{-1}\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b14cf1e4-785f-5b17-867e-45e5d7cc5a9f" :answer/id #uuid "b14cf1e4-785f-5b17-867e-45e5d7cc5a9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=BA\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8afcf5b9-6023-5abe-9e32-15e5a0353825" :answer/id #uuid "8afcf5b9-6023-5abe-9e32-15e5a0353825" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}A\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186092406 :activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
